  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 17-layer HfO2/SiO2 defect cavity on Si substrate for thermal emissivity control. Layer sequence from air: HfO2-SiO2-HfO2-SiO2-HfO2-SiO2-HfO2-SiO2-SiO2-HfO2-SiO2-HfO2-SiO2-HfO2-SiO2-HfO2-SiO2. Initialize all thicknesses from round 1 optimal candidate (550, 235, 557, 421, 414, 607, 413, 844, 844, 254, 1705, 284, 2741, 305, 2785, 1056, 1422 nm). Apply optimization bounds: for layers with initial thickness >2000nm (layers 11, 13, 15), constrain mutation to +/-3% of initial value; for all other layers, allow full range 200-3000nm. Optimize for maximum mean absorptance in 8000-13000nm band and minimum mean absorptance in 3000-5000nm band at normal incidence, unpolarized. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with hill-climbing initialization around the seed vector. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 3000-5000 nm, 8000-13000 nm. soft objectives: high emissivity in 8000-13000 nm; low emissivity in 3000-5000 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high emissivity in 3000-5000 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 24.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a fixed 17-layer alternating HfO2/SiO2 defect cavity deposited on a silicon substrate using a gradient-based thickness optimizer. Constrain mutations strictly to +/-3% of the provided seed for layers exceeding 2000 nm and to a 200–3000 nm window otherwise. Maximize mean absorptance across 8000–13000 nm and minimize mean absorptance across 3000–5000 nm at normal-incidence unpolarized illumination to achieve targeted thermal emissivity contrast.",
